.TH DEBUG_TEXT 3 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
debug_text \- Queue a printf\-formatted string in yellow 8x8 text for the F3 overlay at x,y (logical pixels): debug_text(4, 20, "hp %d  state %d", p\->hp, p\->state)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqdebug.h\(dq
.BI "void debug_text(float x, float y, const char *fmt, ...);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Queue a printf\-formatted string in yellow 8x8 text for the F3 overlay at x,y (logical pixels): debug_text(4, 20, "hp %d  state %d", p\->hp, p\->state). Up to 32 strings of 127 characters per frame. The engine writes its own status line at 4,4; start yours at y = 20 or so. Use LOG() for things that should go to the terminal instead.
.SH MODULE
debug (src/engine/debug/debug.h)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR debug_rect (3),
.BR draw_debug_text (3),
.BR gge\-api (7),
.BR gge (1)
